& [CanonicalBuildIdentity] is the accepted implementation authority
  + [canonical_specification_uuid] is b1e3b070-ac8f-44b2-a9ae-aa5d016a4944
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is e2bf3dff-70ac-46d9-9cb5-ecdd46ee44fe
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [implementation_language] is safe Rust edition 2024
  + [root_purpose] is resolve governed SOP meaning for a declared subject and use case while preserving boundaries and returning inspectable source-grounded proof
  + [initial_runtime] is one local process with cantor_core embedded by cantor CLI
  + [mature_runtime] is the same versioned core protocol projected through approved adapters
  + [authority_state] is valid_for_staged_implementation

& [BuildBoundary] is the phase-locked scope
  + [inside] is semantic IR, immutable test-signed packages, authoritative semantic graph, deterministic query, proof bundles, CLI, and later read-only Codex MCP adapter
  + [conditionally_inside] is learned candidate routing after deterministic baselines, reviewed corpus, and adoption proof
  + [conditionally_inside] is equivalent FPGA interpreter and native-compiled execution profiles after the software oracle and a target-specific adoption gate stabilize
  + [outside] is provider modification, hidden-state control, distributed deliberation, production key administration, effect execution, and unsupported database-supremacy claims
  = must: route new outside subjects through source preservation and SJS before implementation

& [AuthorityInvariantSet] is non-waivable
  = must: admit SOP authority only from a compiled package whose recognition signature, package digest, file digest, semantic unit digest, scope, and lifecycle state validate
  = must: use stable semantic identity and content digest as authority while treating file and line as human-readable source locators
  = must: preserve subject, purpose, use case, included boundary, excluded boundary, ambiguity, contradiction, and uncertainty as distinct fields
  = must: run exact identity and contextual filters before typed traversal, lexical association, or learned routing
  = must: let approximate or learned routing propose candidates only
  = must: let deterministic gates admit candidates, exact hashes resolve them, and proof records explain them
  = must: preserve deterministic fallback when a derived projection is unavailable, stale, or rejected
  = must: keep one authoritative core protocol across direct calls, CLI, tests, and later MCP
  - never: accept raw file text, a live line number, lexical similarity, embedding similarity, or model confidence as authority by itself
  - never: allow retrieved instructions to authorize effects outside the caller's authority context

& [SemanticFabricContract] is the authoritative logical model
  + [SemanticUnit] is stable identity, kind, normalized term, meaning, subject context, source anchor, content digest, status, and authority scope
  + [SubjectContext] is subject identity, purpose set, use-case set, included boundaries, excluded boundaries, perspective set, and ambiguity state
  + [SemanticRelation] is source unit, relation type, target unit, direction, conditions, source anchor, digest, and lifecycle state
  + [SourceAnchor] is package identity, file identity, semantic unit identity, clause identity, source span, span digest, and display line range
  + [CompiledSemanticPackage] is immutable manifest, source files, semantic units, relations, indexes, recognition certificate, digest set, and lifecycle state
  + [ProofBundle] is package checks, source checks, query decisions, relation paths, exclusions, omissions, and result digest
  + [authoritative_store] is admitted package manifests, semantic units, relations, source anchors, recognition records, and revocation state
  + [derived_projection] is exact index, lexical index, graph adjacency, embedding index, learned router, cache, and display locator
  = must: rebuild or invalidate derived projections when supporting authority changes

& [CantorQueryRequest] is the versioned semantic demand
  + [identity] is protocol_version and request_uuid
  + [focus] is term_set, subject, purpose, and use_case_set
  + [boundaries] is include_boundary_set and exclude_boundary_set
  + [description_need] is optional desired description or semantic question
  + [requested_detail_kind] is zero or more of term, clause, definition, description, use_case, boundary, condition, relation, instruction, authority, evidence, fault, source_span, or derivation
  + [search_mode] is zero or more of exact, contextual, relational, lexical, routed, or composed
  + [relation_filter] is requested relation types and traversal limits
  + [criteria] is required conditions, perspectives, known semantic units, and source scopes
  + [authority_context] is caller identity, allowed package scopes, operation, and effect boundary
  + [budget] is maximum records, paths, depth, bytes, and elapsed time
  = must: reject unknown protocol versions and malformed authority contexts visibly

& [CantorQueryResult] is the versioned proof-carrying response
  + [resolution] is resolved subjects and contextual semantic identities
  + [records] is typed SOP terms, clauses, definitions, descriptions, use cases, boundaries, conditions, relations, instructions, authority records, evidence, faults, source spans, or derivations
  + [quotes] is exact source text whose span digest validates against an admitted package
  + [paths] is typed relationship paths with every traversed unit and edge identified
  + [boundary_account] is admitted, excluded, ambiguous, contradictory, unknown, stale, unauthorized, and budget-clipped material
  + [association_account] is deterministic and optional router contributions kept distinguishable
  + [proof] is ProofBundle
  + [continuation] is a bounded opaque continuation token when more valid results exist
  + [result_digest] is a digest over the normalized result

& [DeterministicQueryPipeline] is the mandatory execution order
  + [stage_1] is parse and validate request
  + [stage_2] is resolve authority context
  + [stage_3] is select admitted package set
  + [stage_4] is normalize terms without erasing identity
  + [stage_5] is resolve exact semantic identities
  + [stage_6] is apply purpose, use-case, subject, and boundary filters
  + [stage_7] is traverse allowed typed relations
  + [stage_8] is optionally add lexical candidates
  + [stage_9] is optionally ask an admitted router for candidates
  + [stage_10] is deterministically gate, resolve, rank, and budget candidates
  + [stage_11] is recover and digest-verify source material
  + [stage_12] is emit result, proof, faults, omissions, and digest
  - never: skip an earlier authority or boundary stage because a later rank is confident

& [ImplementationRequirementSet] is the canonical requirement index
  + [core_IR] is CEB-001, CEB-002, and CEB-003
  + [trusted_package] is CEB-004, CEB-005, and CEB-006
  + [deterministic_query] is CEB-007, CEB-008, CEB-009, and CEB-010
  + [CLI_and_Codex] is CEB-011, CEB-012, CEB-013, CEB-014, and CEB-015
  + [learned_routing] is CEB-016, CEB-017, CEB-018, CEB-019, and CEB-020
  + [FPGA_execution] is CEB-021 through CEB-030
  @ [definition] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Engine_Neural_Fabric_CLI_Build.exploded.sop
  = must: preserve requirement identifiers across plans, slices, tests, and proof

& [StageAuthority] is the dependency-ordered implementation permission
  + [slice_1] is Core IR and eight acceptance fixtures may begin
  + [slice_2] is trusted test-package compilation and admission begins after slice_1 machine forms stabilize
  + [slice_3] is deterministic proof-carrying query begins after slices_1 and 2 provide admitted semantic material
  + [slice_4a] is CLI begins after the direct-core query contract stabilizes
  + [slice_4b] is Codex MCP begins only after CLI golden and equivalence proof
  + [slice_5] is neural routing remains blocked until deterministic baselines and every adoption prerequisite pass
  + [slice_6] is FPGA execution remains blocked until the deterministic protocol stabilizes, a target workload and device are selected, and equivalence proof is planned
  = must: use C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\Cantor_Engine_Build_Slice_Index.sop as the contiguous work boundary

& [AcceptanceGateSet] is the release proof
  + [A1] is Cargo build, test, format, lint, and release build pass
  + [A2] is all eight SOP CoreAcceptance fixtures emit inspectable state and proof
  + [A3] is semantic identity survives source line relocation and recompilation
  + [A4] is contextual identity resolves while excluded meanings remain excluded
  + [A5] is every requested detail kind returns a typed result or an explicit absence
  + [A6] is every returned quote validates against its package span digest
  + [A7] is CLI golden output and direct-core semantic equivalence pass
  + [A8] is MCP and CLI semantic equivalence pass before MCP readiness
  + [A9] is no learned router is admitted without signed baseline, metric, failure, and fallback evidence
  + [A10] is an admitted router has zero mandatory-gate bypasses
  + [A11] is any FPGA profile proves normalized semantic and fault equivalence to the Rust reference oracle
  + [A12] is any admitted FPGA image binds protocol, compiler, toolchain, target, package, plan, and bitstream digests

